mod:unwrap_param_store_faces;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 1: DEF-671, P11 with the unwrap walk's fuel end failing closed). A STORE THROUGH AN OPTIONAL OR `Result` PARAMETER'S
// UNWRAP IS A STORE INTO WHAT ITS POINTER POINTS AT, the caller's. The escape side peels the unwrap as alias.npk's `passed_pointee` does
// (`escape_unwrap_root`: `??!`, `?!`, `??`, level by level to the parameter's name), through `.value` and a storing callee handed the wrapper whole, so
// the callee's summary records the store and the caller's view across the call is refused. Past 64 unwrap levels the walk's end refuses the store itself
// (BORROW-009). One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main (acb78ea) and reads freed heap there (236 at -O0 and
// -O2 on roads 0-2, 97 under the detector); each is refused by this row. The guards are in unwrap_param_store_guards.npk, the prices in
// unwrap_param_store_prices.npk, the right controls in tests/backend/programs/unwrap_param_store_ok.npk.
// THE FACES (113): P10's closures, kept by P11 (99), from seat A's, seat P's, seat A2's and seat P2's cells and cells-e134: `fu_n64`, `b_obr`, `b_omid`,
// `b_omido`, `b_oswap`, `c_dyn`, `c_gen`, `c_meth`, `c_oloc`, `c_optl2`, `c_opt`, `c_wrap`, `c_wrapr`, `c_wrapu`, `c_wrapv`, `d_call`, `d_fld2`,
// `d_list`, `d_locbr`, `d_rcall`, `d_rfld`, `d_rlist2`, `d_rlit`, `d_rtern`, `d_rvo`, `d_setopt`, `d_tern`, `d_unw`, `e_lpv`, `e_slvres`, `u_lel`,
// `u_lelr`, `u_oro`, `u_pp2`, `u_qqp`, `u_ro`, `u_rvd`, `u_rvl`, `u_rv`, `u_rvo`, `u_sfl`, `u_sfn`, `u_sf`, `u_t2ul`, `u_t2u`, `u_ut`, `b3_ro`,
// `b3_rr3`, `b3_tern2`, `b4_cast2`, `d2a_loc`, `d2a_res`, `d2c_ret`, `l_mut`, `l_opt`, `l_res`, `l_ro`, `lr_opt`, `m_three`, `r1_mut`, `r1_opt`,
// `r1_res`, `w_loc`, `w_whole`, `u_tA_f`, `u_tE_f`, `u_tF_f`, `fu_n1`, `fu_n2`, `fu_n63`, `c_opt2n`, `c_opt2`, `c_optc`, `c_optl`, `c_optn`, `c_res`,
// `b_carg`, `b_loc2`, `b_loc`, `b_pderef`, `b_res2`, `b_res`, `b_targ`, `c4_opt`, `c4_resd`, `c4_res`, `o_2lv`, `o_bind2`, `o_br`, `o_cal`, `o_cast`,
// `o_gen`, `o_loop`, `o_lw`, `o_resn`, `o_tern`, `s_optl`, `u_optl`, `y_opt2`.
// The read-target road's Optional closures (P11 over P10, 8): `x_rt3_nest`, `x_rt_dq`, `x_rt_loc`, `x_rt_nest`, `x_rt_res`, `x_rt_resv`, `x_rt_tern`,
// `x_rt_ue`.
// THE WALK'S FUEL END (2): `fu_n65`, `fu_n66`, a store through 65 and 66 nested `?!` over a `Result` parameter, refused at the walk's end; at 64 and
// below the caller is refused at the call (`fu_n64` here).
// CASTS ABOVE THE UNWRAP (1, a new closure): `ex_c62`, a store through `<-` and 62 casts `=>! HPO->` over `(r ?! E5) ?! E5`, 63 hops of
// `esc_place_root`: main accepts it and reads freed heap (236 at -O0 and -O2, 97 under the detector); refused at the call here.
// THE HOPS' END ABOVE AN UNWRAP (1, no face): `ex_c63`, the same store through 63 casts, 64 hops: refused on main and here alike at `esc_place_root`'s
// hops' end (BORROW-007) and nowhere else, so the unwrap walk adds no store past that end (`r.exhausted`).
// AN OPTIONAL POINTER VALUE NO PLACE NAMES, ITS TARGETS RETYPED BY A CAST (2, new closures): `o16a`, `o16b`, the ternary of two Optional fields handed
// to a callee taking that Optional and storing two or three levels down (177d2b6's `h_rapc` and `h_mix` forms): main accepts each and reads freed heap
// (236 at -O0 and -O2, 97 under the detector); refused at the growth here.
// Left out as duplicates by text: 101 copies of these cells in other folders (the same names), each named in the row's record.
error:E5;
